count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/74-kyeudo","name":"Kyeudo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar74_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1723"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-30T01:31:41-07:00","id":497230,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/411718-inspirational-art-exalted-3e-edition?p=496933#post496933\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What, other people can comment without being told off for it, but<i> I </i>can't?</div> </div> </div> </div></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Alucard, I like you and all, but your comments were making points about how things people were saying they draw on for inspiration did not exactly resemble the things they inspired, and... of course they don't, it's inspirational art, not &quot;this is the things that are in Exalted&quot; art. You might as well take issue with the <i>entire gameline</i> being inspired by Tales of the Flat Earth despite things like the demons all being humanoid, the gods being apathetic glass things, and the world having an open volcano in it.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Comments others have made have been to agree with things being worthwhile sources of inspiration; it's... qualitatively different, in a few ways.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/411718-inspirational-art-exalted-3e-edition?p=496891#post496891\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"http://jessicafongarts.tumblr.com/post/117651451281/opal-print-is-pretty-much-done-and-will-be\" target=\"_blank\">Definitely this.</a></div> </div> </div> </div>I've been thinking that the Crystal Gems in general might serve as a good inspiration for how, even when they're whimsical and kind of pleasant, the raksha are weird and alien.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-01T14:45:05-07:00","id":499408,"title":"","content":"The MTG Khans of Tarkir block has a lot of cool art which is appropriate for Exalted, I think\u200b<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://www.artofmtg.com/wp-content/uploads/2014/09/Khans-of-Tarkir-Art-141.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> \u200b<img src=\"http://www.phdgames.com/wp-content/uploads/2014/08/jeskai2b.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> \u200b<img src=\"http://1.bp.blogspot.com/-cumYRVBqksQ/U_zZu7XB_uI/AAAAAAAAXxg/HVb2YZz_xJM/s1600/khans%2Btarkir%2BMARDU%2BArt.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> \u200b<img src=\"http://media-dominaria.cursecdn.com/attachments/128/741/635360994392002965.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/117-solar","name":"Solar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-01T15:20:00-07:00","id":499440,"title":"","content":"I keep wondering where oversized pack animals (like, beyond even the yeddim) belong in Exalted. It doesn't really feel fitting to the general aesthetic of the First Age to me. I thiiiink... I could see it as something the Fair Folk bring to war.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"a