"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-27T00:22:48-07:00","id":1153416,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Clophiroth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/411718-inspirational-art-exalted-3e-edition?p=1153119#post1153119\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My current campaign is in an Egypt-expy area (with a Nubia-expy and a Israel-mixed-with-Carthage-expy in the area, but the two main kingdoms are basically Pharaonic Egypt and Theocratic Egypt) so, I\u00b4m really really grateful for these images <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I recommend you check the image links in my signature. All of the pictures I posted in this thread can be found there, but there are dozens of others and you might find something useful for your campaign.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Ultimate Jade-Screened Exalted Scholar, Savant of the Immaculate Texts, No Moon Scholar<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1304239-my-next-campaign-tdhr-peach\" target=\"_blank\">THDR : Future Dragon-Blooded campaign</a>, and other links.<br /> If you like Ex3, you can support <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/holdenshearer\" target=\"_blank\">Holden</a> on Patreon!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/541-letipex","name":"LeTipex","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar541_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"902"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-27T07:08:48-07:00","id":1153467,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sagara</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/411718-inspirational-art-exalted-3e-edition?p=1152724#post1152724\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm gonna dare a bit too - got something with a Pharaonic Egypt feel?</div> </div> </div> </div>Quick and dirty tip: MtG has had fantastic art in the last few years, and there were entire sets dedicated to decidedly non-European visual influences. If nobody in your group is familiar with it, you should just shamelessly use whatever you can out of the Amonkhet set (which is probably not called that, but I don't play the damn thing, I'm just in for the pretty pictures). Examples:<br /> <br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://i.pinimg.com/736x/a9/f5/57/a9f5579f74879a1c6532df07936e5177--black-fantasy-characters-amonkhet-art.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://68.media.tumblr.com/96a73e609b8de69e1516c15071450533/tumblr_ooep334nUB1r3bmeoo1_1280.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://www.artofmtg.com/wp-content/uploads/2017/03/Loyal-Retainers-Invocations-Amonkhet-MtG-Art.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://s3.gatheringmagic.com/uploads/2017/05/03/ML_1.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> Helpful resources: <a href=\"https://hu.pinterest.com/davidedgarotto/scena-egiziano/?lp=true\" target=\"_blank\">this pinterest</a>, <a href=\"http://www.gatheringmagic.com/mikelinnemann-05032017-amonkhet-art-review/\" target=\"_blank\">this art review page</a> (pretty much all of the land art is usable environmental art), <a href=\"http://www.artofmtg.com/set/hour-of-devastation/\" target=\"_blank\">maybe this one too</a> (probably not exhaustive).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=943303#post943303\" target=\"_blank\">Evocations for the demonic tattoos gained from the Pact with Mara sorcerous initiation</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907071#post907071\" target=\"_blank\">Pyre-Kindler (Soulsteel and Red Jade Grimscythe, Artifact 3)</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1072019-soulsteel-stormcaller-concept-gravedigger?p=1074897#post1074897\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Descent (Stormcaller's Black Jade Reaver Daiklave cousin, Artifact 5)</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1074256-combat-with-corebook-shikari-antagonists?p=1074303#post1074303\" target=\"_blank\">Advice for running the corebook shikari antagonists</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","name":"aluminiumtrioxid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3443_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-06T02:56:05-08:00","id":1156268,"title":"","content":"WHERE WERE ALL THESE AMAZING PICTURES WHEN I WAS PLANNING MY EGYPTIAN STYLED SOUTHERN CAMPAIGN TWO YEARS AGO?!?! WHAT DO YOU MEAN I COULD HAVE SEARCHED FOR IT MYSELF?!?! <br /> <br /> Seriously, thanks - that collection is awesome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Visit me at <a href=\"http://www.bragrman.com\" target=\"_blank\"><i>Tales of Grey</i></a> - my RPG Game-Master's blog.<br /> <br /> &quot;If only I had an enemy bigger than my apathy, I could have won&quot; - <i>I gave you all,</i> Mumford &amp; Sons","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8520-capitantypo","name":"CapitanTypo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8520_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"896"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-06T03:36:43-08:00","id":1156274,"title":"","content":"Amonkhet only came out this year.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-06T15:06:09-08:00","id":1156493,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/411718-inspirational-art-exalted-3e-edition?p=1156274#post1156274\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Amonkhet only came out this year.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then I don't feel so useless.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Visit me at <a href=\"http://www.bragrman.com\" target=\"_blank\"><i>Tales of Grey</i></a> - my RPG Game-Master's blog.<br /> <br /> &quot;If only I had an enemy bigger than my apathy, I could have won&quot; - <i>I gave you all,</i> Mumford &amp; Sons","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8520-capitantypo","name":"CapitanTypo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8520_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"896"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-06T19:43:17-08:00","id":1156549,"title":"","content":"That red-violet mummy fellow looks Incan rather than Egyptian to me. Though that reduces his awesomeness not one bit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-08T06:51:02-08:00","id":1156984,"title":"","content":"I must add, albeit this veers a little off-medium, the <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=EbBHk_zLTmY&amp;list=PLhyKYa0YJ_5Aq7g4bil7bnGi0A8gTsawu\" target=\"_blank\">Extra History </a>and <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=jd9Baab9Xsc&amp;list=PLhyKYa0YJ_5AW7F7lD_cGWqxbWIIWIfup\" target=\"_blank\">Extra Scifi</a> studies.<br /> <br /> The first is <b>CRAMMED</b> with amazing events surrounding amazing people. Most could easily fall into what we expect of the Exalted. It's also huge (the playlist has it all on release order). Start with our resident supernal war dawn Hannibal Barca and the punic wars!<br /> <br /> The second... the second is what made me post. It started last week, a study on why sci fi is what it is and what its roots are. Stories of Excellence, Passion, Hubris! It's little surprise that such roots are fundamental to Exalted. And if such tenets matter to you (one would expect so, for this is the exalted forum!) you might like what you'll see. My particular love for sci fi and for exalted nearly brought me to tears as I watched the second episode (i'm weird. don't judge).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-08T08:38:45-08:00","id":1157020,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt the Bruins fan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/411718-inspirational-art-exalted-3e-edition?p=1156549#post1156549\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That red-violet mummy fellow looks Incan rather than Egyptian to me. Though that reduces his awesomeness not one bit.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would have said Aztec or Mayan but yeah definitely a mesoamerica/Inca style. The square spirals and the bright blue feathers","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-21T14:44:16-08:00","id":1169479,"title":"","content":"Some more images!<br /> <br /> <br /> L5R has gorgeous art, but it's best used in moderation: &quot;aesthetically, this game draws from Asian influences&quot; has an unfortunate tendency to translate as &quot;all Japanese, all the time&quot; in players' heads, which really undersells the breadth and diversity of Creation. <i>That said</i>, I don't think anybody could find a finer picture for a Single Point stylist than this one:<br /> <br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://i.pinimg.com/originals/0b/fe/e4/0bfee489f3115924085d1ecee40dee57.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> <br /> While we're on the subject of badass warrior women, here's someone who <i>actually looks like</i> she has Strength 5:<br /> <br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://i.pinimg.com/736x/c3/55/4e/c3554ec741f424907fb1c80618c95c8c--character-inspiration-character-art.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> <br /> Back to L5R: pictures that lack clear identification of actually being from L5R (so basically the ones without katanas and massive clan symbols) can usually be slotted in without worrying too much about breaking the intended aesthetics. So have a merchant. You can never have too many merchants and bureaucrats - images of courtiers are easy enough to find in my experience, and you rarely need pictures for peasants, but merchants are the kind of everyman type that's really easy to run out of.<br /> <br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://78.media.tumblr.com/tumblr_maimicotrI1r2yvruo1_1280.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> <br /> Last but not least: alternate Blood Ape art, if you want something with a bit more flair than the corebook version:<br /> <br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://img00.deviantart.net/32fb/i/2016/044/b/9/orangutan_creature_design_by_dongjunlu-d9rkhnp.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=943303#post943303\" target=\"_blank\">Evocations for the demonic tattoos gained from the Pact with Mara sorcerous initiation</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907071#post907071\" target=\"_blank\">Pyre-Kindler (Soulsteel and Red Jade Grimscythe, Artifact 3)</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1072019-soulsteel-stormcaller-concept-grav