2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-02T21:46:46-08:00","id":1172909,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DraMaFlo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/411718-inspirational-art-exalted-3e-edition?p=1172792#post1172792\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the author is Chinese and they use the same word for both, or rather gorilla is called big orangutan</div> </div> </div> </div>According to wiktionary, &quot;ape&quot; or xingxing is generally considered to mean gibbon or orangutan because of historical geographical reasons. Gorillas are specifically daxingxing (large ape).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-03T02:11:23-08:00","id":1172950,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure if this goes here or if I should just start a whole sandsverse thread, but this playlist has been a massive source of inspiration for me as I make Exalted plans: <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/playlist?list=PLrAx5UkCHzO4JoGDTQ5gHdOlaQN95d87J\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.youtube.com/playlist?lis...gHdOlaQN95d87J</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1170342-truth-machine-chronicle-planning-thread\" target=\"_blank\">The Truth Machine Chronicle</a> - A first-time Exalted campaign.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/20988-socratease","name":"Socratease","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"37"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-10T13:18:31-08:00","id":1174963,"title":"","content":"This person's rendition of the Legend of Zelda character Din, the Goddess of Power:<br /> <img src=\"https://img00.deviantart.net/86ec/i/2016/020/3/3/commission_for_squeaky_pickle___din_by_sockpoppet-d9oo1ia.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> I just think it's a nice design, particularly the golden writing on the tongue.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-26T20:27:12-08:00","id":1179711,"title":"","content":"This image<br /> <img src=\"https://i.pinimg.com/originals/d9/86/b1/d986b191b9144e449be46e6e4fb333a7.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> \u200bstrikes me as something very fitting to the Underworld, particularly the Labyrinth or one of those Deathlord citadels they make by provoking the Neverborn to erupt from the ground.<br /> <br /> \u200bI mean, the death associations are fairly obvious, with the bones and the blood and the corpses, and even the funereal feel of candles and alters and what look like sarcophagi. <br /> <br /> \u200bBut for me personally, it also strikes a good balance between something that might be conventional horror, and something more sombre and ambiguous. It's a twisted image, but I don't think it would be noisy or in your face about it. It constructs its horror out of deathly motifs, and then seems to be quietly reflective. It covers a few bases there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-02T22:25:37-08:00","id":1181917,"title":"","content":"The ongoing sequential art series <a href=\"https://www.artstation.com/mattrhodes/albums/77988\" target=\"_blank\">Tellurion</a>, from artist Matt Rhodes. A mortal falls into the company of a brass legionnaire, seeking an ancient sword. (Post 1 of 2)<br /> <br /> Spoilered on account of the image's size:<br /> <br